News - How to Tell if Shoes Are Slip-Resistant Before You Buy
There are a few simple tricks you can try.
Before you even put the shoes on, check the box. Some boxes will note if the shoes are slip resistant.
Shoes that are oil-resistant or slip-resistant will have a specific tread to them. This tread can come in different shapes such as circles or hexagons.
Look for a rubbery sole that will stick to the ground.
A lot of online stores that sell slip-resistant work shoes will offer guarantees and money back if the shoes fail. They might have tested their shoes as well and posted their results.
