We remember the different Types of maintenance that exist and of which we have already spoken and some techniques such as RCM
Dynamics like that of Quality circles within the production of a company they are being implanted to the maintenance.
With automation and the introduction of robots (Factory Automation) the necessary technical capacity has been increased in line operators, but above all in maintenance. More and more technically trained personnel are needed.
Initially, the RCM was implemented to the aeronautical industry, where these replacement costs were much more expensive, which generated major economic problems for companies in the sector. Later it was expanding to other fields of the industry due to the great success it had in the aforementioned sector.
By example, maintenance operations must know the temperature or range of operating temperatures tolerated by a system, the pressure, maximum accepted vibration, the number of cycles it accepts before breaking, hours of work, know the possible failures that it could have, etc. .
El Preventive Maintenance it is somewhat sophisticated, and involves interventions to prevent failures. In this case, they are based on the reliability of the equipment, and depending on the case, the industrial maintenance tasks will be carried out in more or less frequent periods of time.
Among the tasks of preventive maintenance, it goes from the simple cleaning of the equipment so that work properly, to the change of worn parts before they fail, change of lubricants, etc., depending on the recommendations of the manufacturer of the machine, or the opinion of experts. Therefore, it also prevents failures before they occur, just like the predictive one.
Currently, the Computerization of maintenance tasks has meant a great leap in quality versus how it was operated in the past. Not only does it allow better control, it also facilitates the prevention of possible failures and the monitoring of parameters that may affect the machine or installation.
In English it corresponds to the acronym CMMS (Computerized Maintenance Management System). Basically it is a software or suite of programs that provides a series of services for the company maintenance.
