This type of machine got greatly improve the quality of the pieces obtained, lower costs, increase productivity, and what is more important, achieve greater homogeneity between the parts produced by these methods. Introduction
That Parsons machine it was nothing more than a milling machine with vacuum valve technology that could be programmed by loading data. Since then, these primitive numerical control machines have evolved into much more precise systems using electronic analog and later digital control technology.
That would make the current computerized numerical control or CNC machines (Computer Numerical Control) in the 70s, laying the foundations for CNC machines as we know them today. Little by little they began to be cheaper and easier to program, until they spread to a multitude of industrial sectors and workshops of all sizes.
Find out what is Industry 4.0 and how this type of technology can be integrated.
Like 3D printers, to be able to carry out these movements they are also used servomotors. You just need the right code or software to program the movements of these servomotors to achieve the magnificent results that these machines have.
Tool: it is the head that acts on the piece.
Drive system and interface: these are the controls by which the machine can be operated or controlled. In addition, the interface can also offer information or monitoring of the process.
Like any system, numerical control machines they have their advantages and disadvantages. Obviously, its advantages are clearly superior, and make it worthwhile to use this type of machining despite the disadvantages in most cases.
Automation makes it possible to control and carry out manufacturing processes without human effort.
It allows to manufacture all kinds of parts and carry out a multitude of processes from raw material to a finished product in some cases.
All these advantages should be weighed in conjunction with its disadvantages:
High initial cost of these machines. Specialization.
Manual: programming is done by entering the information you want in a shell. It is done using an alphanumeric code, such as that of the DIN 66024 and 66025 standard.
Evidently nowadays those that have been imposed for their advantages and ease of use are the automatic ones.
El APT language, Through which CNC machines are programmed, it is a high-level programming language that is used as intermediate code before being translated into machine code so that it can be interpreted by the machine.
It is considered as the predecessor of modern CAMs (Computer-Aided Manufacturing), and it shares many similarities with other ancient programming languages such as FORTRAN. His job is to use the data from the programs to handle the numerical control machines with them.
HR APT instructions they can refer to a multitude of controls on the numerical control machine.
Auxiliary functions such as rotation, programmed stop, if the tool has to be changed automatically ...
Obviously, current systems make it possible for operators not to have to know the APT language, but rather the software will take care of everything so that the process is done transparently. Part designers just have to focus on creating the part they want with CAD-like programs.
Basically it is a computer connected to a network in which there is one or more CNC machines. Before it used to be used serial communications type RS-232C or RS422, but new communication technologies have improved these interfaces towards Ethernet, and even wireless.
