WMS or WMS: Put a warehouse management system in your company
Key points to improve a company's storage system and streamline working methods. This is important in a small-medium warehouse, but it is even more so in large warehouses, where human capacity is not enough to keep an absolute control of everything.
With thousands of square meters, hundreds of operators, and with the capacity to manage more than 180.000 packages per day. A titanic logistical task that would be impossible without Amazon's best kept secret, its own SGA software.
There are not many types of SGA, only 3 fundamentals. In addition, they do not have too much mystery, you just have to know that there are these three fundamental variants:
integrated: are those that are integrated into other systems, such as ERP. They allow you to have a centralized system for all aspects of the company, which can be a great advantage.
ModulesSome are presented as modules that can be added to other software packages. Of course, as is often the case with many software packages, there are also systems integrated in the cloud (SaaS) ready to use when you need them without having to install anything locally, free and open source SGA systems, as well as free ...
A very recurring doubt What comes up is what is the best package or SGA solution. As with any software, there are several alternatives available, and although the differences are not too great in some cases, there may be details that make the difference between one software and another.
Fishbowl Inventory: very provisional software with the ability to extend its capabilities through plugins. Its price is about $ 4,395 per user and annually, so it is not a cheap solution for SMEs.
Ideal for the food industry, sanitary, manufacturing, etc. 3PL Warehouse Manager: professional software specially designed for vendors in the e-commerce, 3PL, retail, and manufacturing industries.
Odoo- One of the best free and feature-free SGA software. In addition to having a large number of functions, it is very flexible and open source.
ZhenHub: this software has a free version limited to 50 orders per month, or an unlimited version for € 29 per month.
The company that uses an EMS will be able to have a software where everything is within reach, without having to have several tools for different tasks. Saving.
All products can be managed in a simple way thanks to a digital and automated system that allows updating the database in real time, to know the available stock, the items that have left, what is needed, etc. This also means savings by not buying material that was not necessary or there are delays when some material has run out without being aware of it.
Advantages for e-Commerce. They are systems that have a special importance for e-Commerce systems, with which they integrate perfectly.
In spite of the initial investment that you need this type of SGA systems, in the case of those that are paid, the investment can be recovered quickly with the reported advantages. Therefore, it will be worth using this type of system.
Again, as with other systems that involve a change in the way of proceeding, it needs to be implemented effectively. Deployment is not easy, and you have to draw up a plan of action so that the initial impact is the least.
Functions that an EMS should have In a SGA software they can be highlighted various groups of basic operations.
Location management: you can manage the correct location of the merchandise within the warehouse so that it is in the ideal place for its conservation and also to be able to manage them. For example, some materials could be dangerous if they are together, so the software can optimize their storage so that they stay apart and the space and order of the warehouse is not compromised too much.
Replacement: It also optimizes the way of moving within the facility, such as cross-docking, but this time it is intended to replenish the stock of products that are few or are sold out.
The GHS software must be capable of give data on the amount of product left in the warehouse (stock). For this, functions such as:
Turnover count and calculation: An EMS system must have an idea of the rotations that have been made on a specific item, count and inventory.
In addition to managing the entry of material and movements within the warehouse itself, the WMS must be able to manage the last stage of warehouse logistics, that is, product outputs (picking). That implies the following:
Labeled. The dispatched material must be correctly labeled to identify and follow the packages until they are delivered.
Load. Of course, the materials, if they are not intangible goods, must be loaded in the transport chosen for delivery.
Some large companies, as I mentioned at the beginning, also choose to develop their own warehouse management software. That allows them to hide some secrets to optimize material and logistics management.
Optimization of material flows for production lines. In this way, the agility of the internal processes of the industry is improved.
Some advanced SGAs also allow multi-organization. In other words, intelligent systems capable of managing several organizations or companies belonging to a group in a unified way.
Some other companies may need specific and adapted developments to your needs. Very particular things that are not common and therefore are not implemented regularly by SGA software developers.
