El Modifying maintenance is possibly the most overlooked and underrated type of maintenance, but it is no less important for our projects and our maintenance plan within any company that wants to work on maintenance in a professional way.
The concept of modifying maintenance includes activities that are not typical of the maintenance department but they are complementary and we must take them into account and work on them.
This requires certain needs, such as the specific training of the operator and also that he accept said responsibility. Because if we simply impose it but the worker does not feel integrated and does not want to participate in the model, it will not work well.
El RCM (Reliability Centered Maintenance), or reliability-focused maintenance, is a technique aimed at developing a plan of maintenance in an industrial plant. This allows obtaining a series of advantages over other techniques, obtaining profitability to avoid having to replace parts more periodically.
El Predictive Maintenance It is one that is based on periodic inspections to determine the status and operability of the equipment and facilities. Technicians dedicated to this type of industrial maintenance will need to have in-depth knowledge of the equipment they are analyzing, and to know a series of factors or variables that can affect these systems.
El maintenance plan programmed is a set of actions or activities specially designed to attend to an installation or machine. In this way, it is intended to prevent the main failures that may occur, although that does not guarantee 100% that they can all be stopped.
The main objective is preserve equipment and facilities. In addition, like the predictive one, it is also usually done with the machinery running, so it does not imply reducing productivity and maintains the high availability so desired in these environments where idle time is very expensive.
If you are reading this you need more information. do not miss these key topics of industrial maintenance The maintenance plan, tools CMMS and Types of maintenance.
El industrial maintenance It is a necessary practice to ensure that all the equipment you work with is in good condition, ensuring productivity and good production quality at all times. Only with a good maintenance policy can failures and possible breakdowns be minimized.
Industrial maintenance is a procedure that brings together a series of standards and techniques to preserve the machinery and facilities of any type of industry or workshop. To achieve a conservation of the machines and tools used, and reduce major breakdowns, you need to have a good policy.
