He describes it as an explosion at every point in space. The name of Big Bang comes from Fred Hoyle, an English astrophysicist, who defended the static universe model and in an interview to make fun of explaining the theory, he called it Big Bang, and with that name it has stayed.
Life did not appear in the oceans, it probably arose in lagoons and swamps, where there was quartz and clay, where the chains of molecules were trapped and there they associate with each other. In this way, the bases from which DNA ends up being formed appear.
