On November 12, 2021, the Eurasian Economic Union Commission (EEC) adopted Resolution No. 130 – “On the procedures for the importation of products subject to mandatory conformity assessment into the customs area of the Eurasian Economic Union”.
From January 30, 2022, when importing products for customs declaration, in the case of obtaining the EAC certificate of conformity (CoC) and the declaration of conformity (DoC), the relevant certified copies must also be submitted when the products are declared. The copy of the COC or DoC is required to be stamped completed “copy is correct” and signed by the applicant or manufacturer (see attached template).
