Which is more suitable for fragile products packaging: air column bag, foam or pearl cotton?
The common fragile packaging in life is roughly Polyamide (i.e. foam), pearl cotton and air column bags, so what kind of packaging to choose to package fragile products?
Logistics delivery: Polyamide, pearl cotton transportation costs are very high, although the weight is small, but the space occupied by a large, slightly on some volume will require many trucks loaded; because the air column bags are not inflated before use, so the transport of such inflatable bags only need a small space, saving a lot of transportation costs.
Environmental protection: polystyrene and pearl cotton is "white pollution", after use is difficult to degrade, difficult to deal with, the combustion of toxic gases; air column bags through the SGS non-toxic certification, in line with the EU ROHS green environmental requirements, high temperature after the sale of non-toxic non-polluting, in line with the seventh category of environmental protection resources recycling.
Through the above comparison can be seen, both in cost control as well as protection performance, etc., in the global increasing attention to environmental issues under the prerequisites, the use of air column bags is the future trend! Fragile goods packaging using air column bags is better.
