"They have healed also the hurt of the daughter of my people slightly, saying, Peace, peace; when there is no peace" (Jeremiah 6:14). Introduction: George Whitefield was born in Gloucester, England in 1714.
His preaching on the absolute necessity of the new birth resulted in the churches closing their doors to him, since carnal pastors were afraid that his sermons on the necessity of the new birth would anger their parishoners. Thus, he was forced out of the churches, to preach in the open fields, for which he became famous.
He was close friends with Benjamin Franklin, Jonathan Edwards and John Wesley, and was the one who persuaded Wesley to preach in the fields, like he did. Benjamin Franklin once estimated that Whitefield spoke to an audience of thirty thousand people.
The following sermon by Whitefield is given in modern English. It is his actual sermon, but I have modified the words to make it more understandable in our time.
Sermon: The greatest blessing God can send a nation is good and faithful preachers. But the greatest curse God can send to any nation is to allow the churches to be run by lost preachers who are concerned only with making money.
God wanted him to tell them that their houses would be destroyed – that war was coming (see Jeremiah 6:11-12). Jeremiah gave a thundering message.
"They have healed also the hurt of the daughter of my people slightly, saying, Peace, peace; when there is no peace" (Jeremiah 6:14). The words of the text refer primarily to outward peace.
You must not only do some things, but you must do all things or you are cursed:
Examine your heart. And let me ask you – was there ever a time when the remembrance of your sins was painful to you?
Could you ever say, "My sins are too heavy for me to bear?" Did you ever experience anything like this?
No! Everything in the world is out of order!
No matter how strongly you may deny this, when you are awakened, you will see that sin in your life comes from your own depraved heart – a heart poisoned by original sin.
Did you ever experience this?
Did you ever come to agree that you are by your very nature a child of wrath? (Ephesians 2:3).
You are unjustified and unconverted by your very nature. You deserve to be damned in Hell ten times over for your outward sins.
"They that are in the flesh cannot please God" (Romans 8:8). It is impossible for an unconverted person to do anything for the glory of God.
Someone may say, "Well, I believe all this." But there is a great difference between "believing" and "feeling."
And can you now say, "Lord, you can damn me for the best religious works I could do." If you have not been brought out of yourself like this, there can be no real peace for you.
I am afraid that you have no more faith in Jesus Christ than the Devil himself. I think the Devil believes more of the Bible than most of you.
If I ask you how long it is since you believed in Jesus Christ, many of you would tell me that you have always believed in Him. You could not give me a better proof that you never yet believed in Jesus Christ.
Jesus Christ said concerning the Holy Spirit: "He will reprove the world of sin…Of sin, because they believe not on me" (John 16:8-9).
Were you ever made to grieve in sorrow over your hard heart of unbelief?
If not, you won't find peace in your heart. May God awaken you, and give you solid peace by faith in Jesus, before you die and have no further chance.
You must not only be convinced of your actual and original sin, the sins of your own righteousness, and the sin of unbelief, but you must be enabled to lay hold on the perfect righteousness of the Lord Jesus Christ. You must take ahold of the righteousness of Christ.
Did Jesus Christ ever give Himself to you?
I pray God that Christ may come and speak peace to you. You must experience these things to be born again.
V.Before you can have peace in your heart, you must lay hold of the righteousness of Christ, Matthew 11:28.
The majority of Spurgeon’s converts were not instant, but started with a few weeks or even months of painful conviction and sorrow before trusting in Christ alone and finding joy and assurance. Here are two testimonies of young ladies that were converted under Spurgeon’s preaching.
“Without shedding of blood is no remission” (Hebrews 9:22).
“Without shedding of blood is no freedom, no pardon, no deliverance, no liberty, no forgiveness.”
“There are some preachers who do not preach about the blood of Jesus Christ, and I have one thing to say to you concerning them: Never go to hear them!
A ministry that has no blood in it is lifeless, and a dead ministry is no good to anybody.”
First, consider what will happen to you without the shedding of Christ’s Blood. Without the shedding of Christ’s Blood there is no freedom from your sin.
Only a gasp for breath, only a stopping of your heart for a single moment, and you will be in an eternal world, without God, without hope, without forgiveness. Oh, can you face it?
I think many cases of heart disease, and other sicknesses, come from the torment of unconfessed and unforgiven sin. The great Puritan scholar John Owen said, “By faith we receive the purifying virtue and influences of the blood of Christ.” But you will never find true peace, for
You may think that no one sees the sins of your heart. But you are wrong.
But thank God there is more in the Bible.
Second, consider what will happen to you if you have the shed Blood of Christ. The Blood of Christ reverses the order of our text.
As Fanny Crosby put it in her wonderful hymn,
Redeemed by the blood of the Lamb;
His child and forever I am.
Sing the chorus with me!
I am giving you the New International translation for clarity: “Be shepherds of the church of God, which he bought with his own blood” (Acts 20:28).
“A bloodless gospel...is a gospel of devils.”
Let modern preachers beware who say the “Blood” is only another word for Jesus’ death – beware!
“Redeemed, How I Love to Proclaim It!” Sing it!
She screamed again and then the demons came out of her mouth, just as they did when Jesus was on earth. After a while that girl was free!
I am sure that Spurgeon himself would have been pleased!
The Blood of Jesus can cleanse any sin of your heart or life!
There exists an essential element of preciousness in Christ’s blood. It flowed from arteries untouched, untainted by the virus of sin...a holy Saviour offering a sinless atonement for unholy, sinful man.
Oh, if I could be nailed on a cross for you this evening, I know what you would do: you would fall down and kiss my feet, and weep and cry out that I died for you. But, lost sinner, Jesus died for you – for you!
Are you convinced of sin because you do not believe fully on Christ?
Trust in Jesus Himself, not that He died for you. But trust Jesus Christ Himself.
Do you know it?
if Jesus were here this evening, He would stretch out His bleeding hands to you, and say, “Sinner, I died for you.
“Oh!” but you say, “I am a bad sinner!” “Oh!” says Jesus, “that is just why I died for you, because you are a sinner.” “But,” you say, “I have done things and thought things that I am ashamed of.” Jesus says, “It is all forgiven, all washed away by the Blood that ran from my hands and feet and side. Only trust in me; that is all I ask.” Trust Jesus Christ Himself.
But do you feel that you are guilty?
Then I can tell you that Christ died for you. Believe in Christ!
Then again I say, ‘Come to Jesus Himself. He will wash away your sins in His precious Blood.’”
To end this sermon I will say there is not a lost sinner in this place, who knows that he is lost, who cannot have all his sins forgiven and “rejoice in the hope and the glory of God.” Though you are as black as Hell in sin, you can be as white as Heaven this very night. The very moment that a sinner believes on Jesus he is saved by the Blood of Jesus.
But that Thy blood was shed for me;
Confess your sins to God. Then trust Jesus, come to Jesus, be washed clean from your sins by the precious Blood of Jesus.
