The first prophecy of the Virgin Birth of Jesus was in the Garden of Eden, a short time after our first parents sinned against God. They had listened to Satan tempt them, and had sinned.
Our opening text is also from the Old Testament. The prophet Isaiah said,
The only woman in history who was a virgin, and was impregnated by supernatural means, was Mary, the mother of Christ.
Second, the Virgin Birth of Christ is proved by the New Testament.
“Behold, a virgin shall be with child, and shall bring forth a son, and they shall call his name Emmanuel, which being interpreted is, God with us” (Matthew 1:23). Joseph was engaged to Mary.
“Behold, a virgin shall be with child, and shall bring forth a son, and they shall call his name Emmanuel, which being interpreted is, God with us” (Matthew 1:23).
I decided to go through the New Testament to see what the people who knew Jesus best thought about His virgin birth. I just jotted down on a piece of paper what people who lived with Him thought.
“Then Joseph being raised from sleep did as the angel of the Lord had bidden him, and took unto him his wife: And knew her not till she had brought forth her firstborn son: and he called his name JESUS” (Matthew 1:24-25). Next, there was Mary.
“And the angel answered and said unto her, The Holy Ghost shall come upon thee, and the power of the Highest shall overshadow thee: therefore also that holy thing which shall be born of thee shall be called the Son of God” (Luke 1:35).
Then, there was Jesus Himself. Jesus Himself said,
I saw that the demons “cried out, saying, What have we to do with thee, Jesus, thou Son of God ? art thou come hither to torment us before the time?” Yes, even the demons knew He was the virgin-born Son of God!
But I have not yet commented on the last part of our text. I will give Isaiah 7:14 as it is quoted from the Septuagint in Matthew 1:23,
It means “God with us.” That is who the virgin-born child is. He is “God with us.”
His name is Emmanuel – God with us! His Blood cleanses us.
“Behold, a virgin shall conceive, and bear a son, and shall call his name Immanuel” (Isaiah 7:14).
But tonight I will give you six errors about revival, things that I have come to believe are mistakes. I hope that these points will help you as you pray for God to send revival.
II. Second, the error that there can be no revival today.
(2) The greatest revival of all will come in the midst of the Great Tribulation, under the Antichrist, at the very end of this age (ref. Revelation 7:1-14).
It is a terrible mistake to think that there can be no revival today!
"And when the Gentiles heard this, they were glad, and glorified the word of the Lord: and as many as were ordained to eternal life believed. And the word of the Lord was published throughout all the region."
I think these two verses clear up the idea that revival depends on our evangelistic efforts. Yes, we are told to "preach the gospel to every creature" (Mark 16:15) - but not every creature will believe!
I know that someone may quote II Chronicles 7:14. But it seems strange that they do not quote a New Testament verse to back up their theory that revival depends on Christians "getting right with God."
Iain H. Murray says, concerning II Chronicles 7:14, "The first thing to say is surely that what is promised is not revival, for the promise has to be understood, in the first instance, in relation to the time in which it was given. It is of Old Testament Israel and her land of which the healing here is spoken" (Murray, ibid., p. 13).
"But we have this treasure in earthen vessels, that the excellency of the power may be of God, and not of us" (II Corinthians 4:7).
V. Fifth, the error that revival is the usual state we should expect in the church. The Holy Spirit was poured out on the Apostles at Pentecost.
"And when they had prayed, the place was shaken where they were assembled together; and they were all filled with the Holy Ghost, and they spake the word of God with boldness" (Acts 4:31).
Some will be converted even when there is no unusual move of God.
We will be instant in season and out of season!
In his book, Revival (Crossway Books, 1992), Dr. Martyn Lloyd-Jones has two chapters, titled "Doctrinal Impurity" and "Dead Orthodoxy." In these two chapters this man, who saw great revival in his early years of preaching, tells us that there are certain doctrines which must be preached and believed if we expect God to send revival.
The Fall and total ruin of mankind - total depravity.
Regeneration - or the new birth - as a work of God, not of man.
Justification by faith in Christ alone - not faith in "decisions" of any sort.
I cannot go into detail, but these are vital doctrines, which must once again be preached if we hope to see revival come to our churches. Our churches are full of lost people, who will never be truly converted unless we preach on these subjects vigorously and strongly - and repeatedly!
“And the Lord God said unto the serpent, Because thou hast done this, thou art cursed above all cattle, and above every beast of the field; upon thy belly shalt thou go, and dust shalt thou eat all the days of thy life: And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel” (Genesis 3:14-15).
The Book of Revelation calls Lucifer “that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world” (Revelation 12:9).
But he could not appear to her as a spirit, for a spirit is invisible.
And so, determined to lead the human race into sin, Satan entered into the body of that reptile.
“And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel” (Genesis 3:15).
The “seed of the woman” can only be a reference to a human descendant of Eve who would have no human father.
By being implanted in the womb of the Virgin Mary, Christ would not inherit the sin nature which would disqualify every son of Adam from being a Saviour from sin.
“The Holy Ghost shall come upon thee, and the power of the Highest shall overshadow thee: therefore also that holy thing which shall be born of thee shall be called the Son of God” (Luke 1:35).
Here we see the perpetual, unending war between the forces of Satan and the forces of Christ.
“In this the children of God are manifest, and the children of the devil: whosoever doeth not righteousness is not of God, neither he that loveth not his brother” (I John 3:10).
“If you were of the world, the world would love its own; but because you do not belong to the world, but I have chosen you out of the world, therefore the world hateth you.” The “world” is the seed of the serpent.
That is why Christians are hated and persecuted today.
If one of them becomes a real Christian, the others will immediately gang up on him and tease him.
“I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed” (Genesis 3:15).
When the lost teenagers in the church see one of their friends become a serious Christian, they will turn from him, talk behind his back, slander him, and deliberately look for faults in him, so they can talk bad about him.
Every child that comes through any church has to go through this test, or they cannot be a real Christian!
Who is on the Lord’s side?
Who will be His helpers, Other lives to bring?
Who will face the foe?
Who for Him will go?
Most adults in the church don’t realize that the Sunday School, or children’s group, is always a fierce battleground between the seed of the serpent and the seed of Christ.
If you are working, you know what I mean. And I am telling you this so you won’t think there is something wrong with you.
What about Christmas?
News commentator Bill O’Reilly calls it “The War on Christmas.” The Governor of an Eastern state refuses to call the state tree a “Christmas tree.” He calls it a “Holiday tree.” There’s been a lot of talk about that.
When she asked if she could do the same for Christmas, she was told “yes.” “Like the other moms, she started by explaining the basis of the holiday by reading from a book.
When she pulled it out, you would have thought she ignited a bomb. The teacher immediately said, ‘Oh, NO!
Senior citizens in Winter Park, Florida were recently banned from singing Christmas carols in their own homes.
In Plano, Texas school officials prohibited children from giving out pencils imprinted with the words “Jesus is the reason for the season.” A school official there even banned children from writing “Merry Christmas” in notes to soldiers in Iraq.
Now it’s always “Happy Holidays.” Whenever anyone says that to me, I always reply, “Merry Christmas!” But it is increasingly clear that the “seed of the serpent” hates to celebrate the birth of Christ, and they attack those Christians who are trying to keep Christmas a Christian holiday!
They say I am a legalistic tyrant for telling you to be in church rather than some dance hall or drunken party.
God said, “I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed...” The “seed of the serpent” will always be against the “seed of Christ.” There’s nothing new about that!
I certainly hope you don’t listen to them!
Or will you be here in church with us?
“I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed...” There is a war going on between the seed of the woman and the seed of the serpent.
This was accomplished when the Lord Jesus died on the Cross, for by dying He honored the law, put away sin, slew death, and defeated Hell!
What can Satan do now?...Christ hath crushed him...the seed of the woman hath broken the power of the enemy!
Did not he himself say, ‘I beheld Satan as lightning fall from heaven’?
Now, I ask you, which side are you on?
Which side are you really on in your heart?
Everyone here this morning is on one side or the other!
And if you wish to speak with us about the salvation of your soul, please leave your seat and step to the back of the room right now.
